From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:59:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(chunks): ignore overlapping subchunk responses

LevelChunk packets can already contain serialized sections while also
requesting additional subchunks. Request only the missing sections, and
keep queued and in-flight requests distinct so each pending section
receives one request.

Ignore repeated subchunk replies once the section is complete, clear
request state on unload, and discard delayed data for replaced chunks.
This prevents a second merge from disconnecting the Java client.

Treat protocol 2193's optional client request limit as a section count,
not the inclusive highest section index used by the older terrain format.
Official 1.26.51.1 client/server captures with limits 1, 2, 5, and 9 request
exactly those counts. Asking for one extra section leaves native-capture
playback waiting forever and withholds all Java terrain. Preserve known-air
sections when replacing a column; its new header owns the request limit.
Bound the count to the dimension and retain unlimited request mode.
A targeted regression covers the captured counts, known air, and dimensions.
